# Git mailmap file to consolidate contributor identities
# See https://git-scm.com/docs/gitmailmap for format details
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> Commit Name <commit@email>
#
# This file ensures consistent contributor attribution across Git history
# by mapping multiple identities (different emails or name variations) to
# a single canonical identity.
#
# This addresses the issue of seeing multiple accounts for the same person,
# which can happen when:
# - Contributors use different email addresses (work vs personal)
# - Name variations in git config (e.g., "First Last" vs "Last First")  
# - Different GitHub accounts are used for different purposes
# - Automated tools (like Snyk) use different account credentials
#
# Note: This file does not modify git history, but changes how Git displays
# contributor information in commands like 'git shortlog', 'git log --author',
# and on some GitHub views.

